Also, note: if I recommend measuring now, the method must be stated precisely: create files at known sizes (e.g., a line of N bytes, unique sentinel at the last line), start an agy session with a trivial prompt asking it to quote the last line, and record the largest size that arrives; a control file under the lowest reported limit; repeat per unit confusion (bytes vs chars). But "Never invent a number": the test sizes should be derived from the two documented figures (12,000 chars, 24,000 bytes) — bisect between them. E.g., use non-ASCII to separate bytes from code units. That's a documented basis.

