- D4: false positives block a commit until waived; the scanner catches only prefixes; the tool now has two jobs and grows; a waived line can hide a real key (the reviewer sees the count, not the value). My #6/#8.
- D5: the measurement costs agy runs and can go stale on an upgrade; it measures one unit/path and not the token budget; if the load path is wrong, the run measures nothing (the control is the guard). My #17/#2.

